WEBVTT

00:07.903 --> 00:13.663
Let's laugh and cry.
chanto waraimasho, nakimasho

00:14.163 --> 00:19.753
Subs originally by Froth-Bite
Manually retyped by #Retrofit@IRC.Rizon.Net
Raws by Darkside-Raws
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha

00:19.753 --> 00:19.793
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha

00:19.793 --> 00:28.343
Making matching memories with you...
anata to osoroi no omoide tsukuruno ga

00:28.343 --> 00:30.213
...is important.
daiji daiji

00:31.593 --> 00:34.143
Sometimes I become...
sunao ni narenakattari

00:34.473 --> 00:37.973
...almost dishonest and mean
ijiwaru shichaisouna hi aruno

00:39.473 --> 00:40.813
That's because...
sore wa...

00:42.813 --> 00:45.563
I love you and adore you,
daisuki de taisetsu de

00:45.693 --> 00:48.903
and I don't want to be apart from you.
hanaretaku nai sei nano nante

00:50.863 --> 00:51.863
That's the truth.
henne

00:54.413 --> 01:01.123
I just want to cuddle...
hontou wa itsumo nuku nuku shitetai

01:01.453 --> 01:03.463
...with you.
futaride

01:04.463 --> 01:10.173
So let's laugh and cry.
dakara waraimashou, nakimashou

01:10.843 --> 01:16.263
We need to keep our hearts warm.
kokoro no ondo wo atatame awanakucha

01:16.473 --> 01:24.773
The fate that made us meet...
anata to deaeta unmei ho subetega

01:24.773 --> 01:26.603
...is important.
daiji daiji

01:40.193 --> 01:42.573
I'm off, Mom!

01:45.903 --> 01:48.163
Bye bye, Kozue Onee-chan!

01:48.743 --> 01:50.953
Have a good day, Asami-chan.

01:50.953 --> 01:57.793
Kozue-chan, we have to get going soon, or we will be late.

02:02.923 --> 02:04.963
Washroom

02:15.223 --> 02:17.563
We'll drink until dawn!

02:17.813 --> 02:19.483
Cheers!

02:19.903 --> 02:22.153
Oh, come on, give me that stuff.

02:22.153 --> 02:23.573
Oh this?

02:23.573 --> 02:23.943
Yup.

02:24.233 --> 02:27.693
Night after night, they party.

02:27.693 --> 02:29.533
I couldn't finish my homework.

02:29.533 --> 02:31.453
What kind of excuse can I make?

02:31.453 --> 02:33.783
Good morning.

02:35.163 --> 02:38.213
Why do you look so tired so early in the morning?

02:38.713 --> 02:40.713
The new semester starts today!

02:40.713 --> 02:42.713
Look sharper!

02:43.003 --> 02:45.343
Whose fault do you think it is?

02:47.303 --> 02:48.223
Whose?

02:51.223 --> 02:54.053
Well, work hard on your education.

02:54.053 --> 02:56.263
So, bye!

02:58.353 --> 02:59.983
I'm off.

03:00.643 --> 03:05.773
Warm and Fuzzy

03:05.773 --> 03:10.363
Kou Design School

03:11.823 --> 03:15.663
Hello, hello, hello, everyone.

03:15.993 --> 03:17.453
Nice to meet you all.

03:17.453 --> 03:23.923
I am your new instructor, Shirogane Miyabi.

03:24.383 --> 03:26.923
I hope you all enjoy my class.

03:27.503 --> 03:29.633
And good luck to you all.

03:29.633 --> 03:31.303
Yes.

03:31.303 --> 03:40.353
So, before we get started, let me collect the "Mar, Mar, Marchen" story character...

03:40.353 --> 03:42.563
...which I asked you to draw to get to know you better.

03:42.893 --> 03:46.613
I can't wait to see what kind of characters you all drew.

03:47.823 --> 03:55.203
I wouldn't imagine that anyone FORGOT this, right?

03:55.203 --> 03:56.283
Uh...

04:01.253 --> 04:04.043
Let's see, you are...

04:04.043 --> 04:05.963
Shiratori Ryoshi-kun, right?

04:05.963 --> 04:07.543
Y-Yes.

04:07.923 --> 04:09.423
You forgot it?

04:09.883 --> 04:11.343
I'm sorry.

04:11.343 --> 04:13.883
I will turn it in tomorrow.

04:13.933 --> 04:15.093
Oh, oh.

04:15.183 --> 04:16.603
Oh my.

04:16.683 --> 04:18.053
What a troublemaker.

04:25.193 --> 04:27.813
Please excuse us for a moment everyone.

04:36.703 --> 04:41.583
Okay, everyone, let me collect the assignments.

04:45.793 --> 04:49.213
I will never forget another assignment again.

04:51.713 --> 04:55.433
Futabadai Station

04:56.803 --> 04:59.473
I'm already starting out in trouble.

04:59.473 --> 05:02.353
You forgot your homework already.

05:02.353 --> 05:04.313
You've got some guts.

05:04.313 --> 05:07.483
I didn't mean to forget it.

05:07.483 --> 05:09.193
Then what?

05:09.193 --> 05:12.613
It's something with the new apartment...

05:12.613 --> 05:15.453
What? Is there some kind of problem?

05:15.653 --> 05:17.663
Like noise or something?

05:17.663 --> 05:18.493
What? What?

05:18.873 --> 05:20.913
Tell us, Shiratori.

05:20.913 --> 05:23.413
Well, I'm not sure if it's a problem...

05:23.413 --> 05:25.253
There are a few unique people...

05:25.253 --> 05:26.963
Oh? Shiratori-san?

05:29.673 --> 05:30.963
Miss Landlady!

05:30.963 --> 05:31.673
Tamami-chan!

05:31.673 --> 05:32.633
What's going on?

05:32.633 --> 05:35.883
Well, you see...

05:35.883 --> 05:39.683
This is the path we take to go to our school every day.

05:41.933 --> 05:44.933
So your school is around here.

05:46.063 --> 05:47.523
Hey, Shiratori.

05:48.063 --> 05:50.903
Is she your friend?

05:50.903 --> 05:55.033
Oh, she is the landlady of the apartment I was just talking about.

05:55.613 --> 05:57.453
Oh, bravo!

05:58.243 --> 06:00.163
God is so unfair.

06:01.073 --> 06:03.033
I wish I had a younger sister like that!

06:04.413 --> 06:08.503
Are you all Shiratori-san's friends?

06:08.503 --> 06:10.383
Yes, we are all from the same class...

06:10.383 --> 06:12.173
Yes, we are friends.

06:12.173 --> 06:14.753
We always work with Shiratori-kun.

06:14.753 --> 06:16.723
Yes, we do.

06:16.723 --> 06:18.093
Nice to meet you.

06:18.093 --> 06:20.473
I'm the landlady of Narutakisou, Aoba.

06:23.723 --> 06:25.523
Everyone,

06:25.523 --> 06:28.313
you are only looking at Kozue-chan...

06:28.893 --> 06:32.813
...and completely... ignoring... me?

06:36.113 --> 06:39.613
Are you already done with school, Shiratori-san?

06:40.613 --> 06:43.623
It's the first day, so they let us out after orientation.

06:43.623 --> 06:46.873
Oh, Miss Landlady, where can I find a bookstore?

06:46.873 --> 06:48.333
A bookstore?

06:49.333 --> 06:52.253
We already have so much homework.

06:52.253 --> 06:53.843
I want to look for a few materials.

06:54.043 --> 06:56.713
Then let me show you.

06:56.713 --> 06:57.343
Are you sure?

06:57.843 --> 06:58.473
Yes.

06:59.423 --> 07:00.473
Thank you.

07:01.093 --> 07:03.093
I'll come too!

07:03.093 --> 07:06.183
It's fine with you, right, Shiratori-san?

07:06.893 --> 07:07.813
Of course.

07:08.223 --> 07:10.853
Then let's hurry!

07:10.853 --> 07:12.483
The landlady is fine,

07:12.483 --> 07:14.943
but I see about the other unique residents.

07:16.693 --> 07:18.323
I heard that.

07:28.873 --> 07:31.163
This place is close to the station,

07:31.163 --> 07:33.463
and you can get most everything you need for daily life.

07:33.833 --> 07:35.963
Of course, there is a bookstore too.

07:36.923 --> 07:38.513
Hey, Kozue-chan!

07:38.963 --> 07:41.423
We've got good daikon radish today!

07:41.423 --> 07:42.683
How about one?

07:45.223 --> 07:49.683
Hey bro, are you Kozue-chan's... "this"?

07:50.523 --> 07:52.273
What is "this"?

07:52.273 --> 07:53.143
I don't know.

07:53.143 --> 07:54.193
Don't play dumb!

07:54.443 --> 07:58.073
I'm asking if this man is your good man.
TL Note: In the Japanese language, when people talk about a girl's good man, they're talking about her significant other. Kozue, being Kozue, takes this phrase quite literally and...

07:58.073 --> 07:58.443
TL Note: In the Japanese language, when people talk about a girl's good man, they're talking about her significant other. Kozue, being Kozue, takes this phrase quite literally and...

07:58.443 --> 08:00.113
Right, bro?
TL Note: In the Japanese language, when people talk about a girl's good man, they're talking about her significant other. Kozue, being Kozue, takes this phrase quite literally and...

08:00.113 --> 08:01.443
Well, uh...
TL Note: In the Japanese language, when people talk about a girl's good man, they're talking about her significant other. Kozue, being Kozue, takes this phrase quite literally and...

08:01.443 --> 08:05.033
Yes! Shiratori-san is a good man.
TL Note: In the Japanese language, when people talk about a girl's good man, they're talking about her significant other. Kozue, being Kozue, takes this phrase quite literally and...

08:09.623 --> 08:10.503
Um...

08:11.203 --> 08:12.293
Miss Landlady!?

08:15.123 --> 08:16.423
I like that!

08:16.423 --> 08:17.173
Here, take this!

08:17.463 --> 08:19.383
It's just a congratulatory gift from me!

08:19.383 --> 08:20.303
Well, but...

08:20.303 --> 08:22.973
Don't be so modest!

08:22.973 --> 08:25.183
Here, take it!

08:25.593 --> 08:27.933
Spring has come for Kozue-chan too.

08:27.933 --> 08:30.353
I'm so happy.

08:30.353 --> 08:33.603
Hey, if you ever make Kozue-chan cry, I'll come get you!

08:33.603 --> 08:34.523
Got that!?

08:34.523 --> 08:35.313
Yes.

08:35.313 --> 08:36.813
My!

08:37.613 --> 08:39.233
He's Kozue-chan's...

08:40.323 --> 08:41.903
...good man?

08:41.903 --> 08:43.073
Yes!

08:43.073 --> 08:45.413
Shiratori-san is a good man.

08:45.413 --> 08:47.453
That's good.

08:47.453 --> 08:49.663
Here, eat this.

08:50.203 --> 08:51.953
Thank you.

08:55.003 --> 08:57.003
Sour!

08:57.713 --> 08:59.713
Oh, Kozue-chan's good man, eh?

08:59.713 --> 09:01.553
Yes, Shiratori-san is a good man.

09:01.553 --> 09:03.513
Oh, Kozue-chan's good man?

09:03.513 --> 09:05.683
Yes, Shiratori-san is a good man.

09:06.053 --> 09:09.723
What's going on with people today?

09:10.053 --> 09:13.853
Did they give us presents because Shiratori-san is a good man?

09:14.393 --> 09:19.153
She doesn't have a clue what they meant by "good man"...

09:19.153 --> 09:22.613
Futabadai Books

09:23.483 --> 09:26.153
They have a good selection of children's books, too.

09:26.613 --> 09:30.453
It's useful to have a good bookstore close to home.

09:33.043 --> 09:34.873
I see...

09:37.793 --> 09:40.633
This is very interesting.

09:47.633 --> 09:51.263
Cooking

09:52.723 --> 09:55.063
Miss Landlady is checking out the cooking books.

09:55.683 --> 09:57.643
A recipe book or something?

09:57.643 --> 10:01.403
Poisonous mushrooms
Delicious Bulbs
Delicious Grasses
Delicious Edible Flowers

10:01.523 --> 10:04.073
What in the world is she reading...

10:04.073 --> 10:05.443
It costs 1,000 yen...

10:05.443 --> 10:06.823
Should I buy it?

10:06.823 --> 10:08.953
And she fully intends to buy it!

10:09.243 --> 10:11.953
Oh, Shiratori-san, good timing.

10:12.953 --> 10:14.953
Which do you think is better?

10:14.953 --> 10:16.873
Survival Cooking

10:16.873 --> 10:17.213
Industrial Pots Collection
Survival Cooking

10:17.213 --> 10:18.463
Industrial Pots Collection

10:18.463 --> 10:20.123
Which?

10:20.123 --> 10:22.713
What are you going to do with those books?

10:24.133 --> 10:26.553
When I get lost in the mountains,

10:26.553 --> 10:29.053
or when I want to give pots as presents,

10:29.053 --> 10:31.473
they might come in handy.

10:32.143 --> 10:33.473
I-I see...

10:39.193 --> 10:42.733
There there, we'll be home soon.

10:45.073 --> 10:46.733
Hello.

10:46.983 --> 10:49.243
How are you?

10:49.863 --> 10:52.953
Miss Landlady, I don't think that's quite appropriate for a baby...

10:58.543 --> 11:02.543
Babies really love cute stuff.

11:03.133 --> 11:04.843
I dunno...

11:11.383 --> 11:13.933
This is so heavy...

11:17.223 --> 11:18.063
Miss Landlady?

11:25.613 --> 11:28.653
Please watch out, Shiratori-san.

11:29.943 --> 11:33.453
Kozue-chan is so warm and fuzzy.

11:39.203 --> 11:40.453
Warm and fuzzy...

11:51.013 --> 11:55.013
Futaba Park

11:55.013 --> 11:58.273
Umeboshi

12:01.443 --> 12:03.943
It feels so good!

12:05.193 --> 12:10.823
This is a place to relax for those who work around here.

12:13.493 --> 12:17.373
It feels like the sky is bigger here.

12:17.993 --> 12:18.833
Yes.

12:19.333 --> 12:21.963
This town has so many buildings,

12:21.963 --> 12:25.293
but this place is filled with flowers and greenery.

12:35.683 --> 12:36.893
What is it?

12:37.813 --> 12:40.143
Oh, it's really nothing.

12:41.523 --> 12:44.403
Am I not wanted here?

12:44.853 --> 12:46.403
Well, uh...

12:47.113 --> 12:48.693
I didn't mean it like...

12:48.693 --> 12:50.323
Are you sure?

12:52.573 --> 12:55.613
I can't find it!

12:56.163 --> 12:58.873
Where did it go?

12:58.873 --> 13:00.413
Excuse me...

13:00.623 --> 13:02.793
Are you looking for something?

13:03.623 --> 13:05.253
Yes, I am.

13:08.923 --> 13:11.013
Your stamp card from the shopping district?

13:12.763 --> 13:15.263
That card was fully stamped.

13:15.263 --> 13:18.473
It was supposed to get me the newest model of futon dryer,

13:18.473 --> 13:22.563
so I can sleep on a soft, warm futon anytime I want.

13:22.563 --> 13:23.683
But...

13:24.563 --> 13:26.523
But...!

13:26.523 --> 13:28.983
Oh boy.

13:31.693 --> 13:34.903
I don't think we can find it with this breeze.

13:38.743 --> 13:41.203
Would you like me to help?

13:43.453 --> 13:44.963
Really!?

13:44.963 --> 13:47.883
Thank you so much, stranger!

13:48.293 --> 13:52.803
If Kozue-chan wants to do it, then I will help too.

13:52.803 --> 13:56.473
Thank you, stranger's friend.

13:59.513 --> 14:01.063
I'll help too.

14:01.063 --> 14:04.233
Thank you, stranger's...

14:05.563 --> 14:07.443
Hey, hey, hey,

14:07.443 --> 14:09.103
is he your good man?

14:10.193 --> 14:13.403
Yes, Shiratori-san is a good man!

14:13.403 --> 14:17.533
Will the lost item be found?

14:18.913 --> 14:20.123
Did you find it?

14:20.123 --> 14:21.993
You are so good.

14:24.583 --> 14:26.463
Are you serious about the search?

14:26.463 --> 14:28.253
Kozue-chan, you're so cute.

14:28.253 --> 14:32.463
Will the lost item be found 2?

14:34.763 --> 14:36.513
Did you find it?

14:36.513 --> 14:38.723
Don't litter in the park.

14:39.893 --> 14:41.973
You're really not serious, are you?

14:42.513 --> 14:46.733
Will the lost item be found 3?

14:46.893 --> 14:48.443
It's not here...

14:48.443 --> 14:49.943
No, it's not...

14:50.403 --> 14:51.153
BAM!

14:51.863 --> 14:52.363
I'm sorry!

14:52.863 --> 14:53.363
I'm sorry!

14:53.363 --> 14:55.993
BLAM!

14:55.993 --> 14:56.943
I'm sorry!

14:57.403 --> 14:58.323
I'm sorry!

14:58.783 --> 14:59.613
I'm sorry!

15:00.243 --> 15:01.453
I'm sorry!

15:04.293 --> 15:06.003
I can't find it.

15:06.453 --> 15:08.543
Maybe it's impossible after all.

15:08.543 --> 15:09.543
It's not here...

15:12.083 --> 15:13.593
Did you find it?

15:14.923 --> 15:16.423
I see.

15:16.423 --> 15:19.133
I guess it's not around here.

15:20.433 --> 15:22.143
What a shocker...

15:22.143 --> 15:25.893
Then I will go look over there again.

15:27.563 --> 15:31.313
I love soft and warm futons too.

15:32.313 --> 15:34.193
How about you?

15:35.653 --> 15:37.363
I like them too.

15:38.653 --> 15:41.703
I hope that someone finds the stamp card.

15:45.913 --> 15:49.333
Futaba Park

15:51.253 --> 15:54.213
Seeing as we couldn't find it after so much searching,

15:54.213 --> 15:58.553
it must have either been blown away or picked up by someone else.

15:58.553 --> 16:00.633
No way...

16:07.433 --> 16:08.683
Not here...

16:09.353 --> 16:12.603
It's best to give up now.

16:13.603 --> 16:15.653
The futon dryer!

16:15.653 --> 16:17.483
The soft futon!

16:17.483 --> 16:21.493
Um, maybe a little longer...

16:21.493 --> 16:22.993
Really!?

16:22.993 --> 16:25.373
Really, you'll look for it a little longer?

16:25.373 --> 16:26.833
Thank you!

16:28.493 --> 16:29.293
Um...

16:31.163 --> 16:33.753
Shiratori-san...

16:33.753 --> 16:36.213
Then let's eat something first.

16:36.843 --> 16:39.763
I have a few cookies I just bought for my snack.

16:42.263 --> 16:44.133
It should be around here...

16:54.693 --> 16:57.193
I'm really sorry!

16:57.193 --> 16:59.613
I really didn't know!

17:00.153 --> 17:02.193
Didn't know?

17:02.193 --> 17:05.453
I thought I had it in my pocket.

17:05.453 --> 17:07.453
I didn't know it was in the basket!

17:07.453 --> 17:09.623
Even God wouldn't know that!

17:10.623 --> 17:14.373
Sure, even God wouldn't have mercy for this.

17:15.713 --> 17:17.333
I'm happy for you.

17:17.333 --> 17:21.343
You didn't lose your stamp card.

17:21.343 --> 17:22.883
I'm really glad.

17:23.383 --> 17:27.343
Thank you so much, stranger!

17:33.143 --> 17:37.153
Jeez, what a troublesome person she was.

17:37.153 --> 17:39.653
But she was a really nice person.

17:40.193 --> 17:42.943
She gave us so much stuff.

17:48.283 --> 17:52.333
If it's sunny next Sunday, let's dry the futon in the sun.

17:52.333 --> 17:55.333
I'm sure it'll smell like the sun and feel good.

17:55.333 --> 17:58.883
I love soft and warm futons too.

18:06.843 --> 18:08.183
Miss Landlady,

18:09.143 --> 18:11.563
do people tell you that you are like spring?

18:12.183 --> 18:14.893
Yes, they do sometimes.

18:14.893 --> 18:16.063
I thought so.

18:17.143 --> 18:18.193
Why is that?

18:18.193 --> 18:20.863
Oh, I just like spring.

18:21.943 --> 18:25.943
Yes, I love spring too.

18:30.573 --> 18:33.833
This is what Tamami-chan was talking about earlier.

18:34.913 --> 18:39.173
It takes everything in, and rounds it all up.

18:40.753 --> 18:43.423
She really is warm and fuzzy.

18:44.343 --> 18:45.133
Narutakisou

18:45.133 --> 18:46.343
We're home!
Narutakisou

18:46.343 --> 18:47.383
We're home!

18:49.763 --> 18:51.643
Welcome home!

18:54.393 --> 18:56.103
We're home, Asami-chan.

18:56.893 --> 18:59.023
You brought home a lot today.

18:59.023 --> 19:01.983
Let's put some daikon in the miso soup tomorrow morning.

19:02.193 --> 19:02.753
Yes.

19:03.273 --> 19:06.403
I'm really glad that Shiratori-san is a good man.

19:06.403 --> 19:09.153
Oh, you know...

19:13.783 --> 19:15.293
It's delicious...

19:21.673 --> 19:23.753
Mom!

19:23.753 --> 19:24.253
Sayoko-san!

19:24.253 --> 19:25.923
Make her cough!

19:25.923 --> 19:27.173
Sayoko-san!

19:27.173 --> 19:28.173
Are you okay!?

19:32.093 --> 19:35.433
Sayoko-san is really troublesome.

19:37.473 --> 19:39.683
I need to finish my homework early tonight.

19:40.693 --> 19:42.103
Welcome home!

19:42.103 --> 19:43.403
We were waiting.

19:44.273 --> 19:46.573
You came into my room without permission again!

19:47.113 --> 19:49.323
That's not a nice way to think.

19:49.323 --> 19:53.373
We were waiting to bless the new life of a young man.

19:55.453 --> 19:57.583
Did anything fun happen?

19:58.583 --> 20:00.003
Not really.

20:00.003 --> 20:01.833
Are you sure?

20:02.623 --> 20:04.173
Tamami-chan!

20:04.173 --> 20:07.843
I have the scoop.

20:12.223 --> 20:13.183
That's...

20:14.303 --> 20:15.893
When!?

20:15.893 --> 20:16.763
What, what!?

20:16.763 --> 20:18.433
What did you take, Tama-chan!?

20:18.433 --> 20:20.063
Let us see too!

20:20.063 --> 20:21.643
Oh, it's nothing.

20:21.643 --> 20:24.063
Oh, let us see!

20:24.653 --> 20:26.233
No, you can't!

20:52.593 --> 20:55.593
Survival cooking

20:55.593 --> 20:58.603
Pot Roast For Big Families

21:01.023 --> 21:04.063
It was another fun day today.

21:18.453 --> 21:21.583
Uh, what about the futon dryer?

21:21.833 --> 21:23.333
That ended last month.

21:23.713 --> 21:26.833
Starting this month, the prize is this chill-chill fridge.

21:26.833 --> 21:29.343
Isn't that great?

21:35.553 --> 21:39.353
My futon dryer!

21:41.643 --> 21:44.563
Warm... soft...

21:57.353 --> 22:03.863
One day, I drew a picture all over a canvas,
itsu no hika canvas ni e ippai

22:03.943 --> 22:09.663
a picture of 7-colored dreams.
nanairo no yume egaita

22:11.083 --> 22:17.543
When I noticed, I was a bit more grown up.
ki ga tsukeba sukoshi otona ni natte

22:17.793 --> 22:22.843
What have I found?
nani wo mitsuketandarou

22:24.803 --> 22:31.553
In this aimless daily life,
yuka ate no nai mainichi no nakade

22:31.803 --> 22:37.483
I found something that's most important.
ichiban taisetsuna koto ni kizuita

22:38.483 --> 22:44.323
Yes, it's always all right,
donna tokidemo sousa daijoubu

22:44.323 --> 22:46.573
because you are here.
kimi ga irukara

22:46.783 --> 22:52.953
Holding these unforgettable thoughts,
wasurenai kono omoi dakishimete

22:53.453 --> 22:59.293
I will start walking the path of the halted fantasy again,
mouichido togireta yume no fantasy

22:59.293 --> 23:03.923
at my own speed.
aruitemiyou boku no speed de

